  <prompt>Correct `docs/data-model/sprk_communication.md`: its `sprk_communicationtype` choice list is missing `Message = 100000004` (present in the shipped `CommunicationType` enum), and the doc omits the R1 messaging columns added by messaging-communication-app-r1 (e.g. the ACS message/thread id columns and the thread lookup). Reconcile the doc to the code + as-built schema; do not touch any source.</prompt>
  <role>SPAARKE platform developer / documentarian. Code is the source of truth; fix the doc to match code.</role>
  <goal>`docs/data-model/sprk_communication.md` lists `sprk_communicationtype` option `100000004: Message` alongside the existing four, and documents the R1 messaging columns present in code (ACS message id / ACS thread id / the `sprk_communicationthread` lookup and any other R1 messaging additions actually in the schema), each with logical name, type, and a short description. The review header/date is updated to note this R3 correction.</goal>
  <context>
    <background>Spec §External Dependencies + plan Phase 1 deliverables call out a doc-drift fix: `docs/data-model/sprk_communication.md` is missing `Message = 100000004` and R1 messaging columns. The shipped enum `src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Communication/Models/CommunicationType.cs` has `Email=100000000, TeamsMessage=100000001, SMS=100000002, Notification=100000003, Message=100000004`, but the doc's `sprk_communicationtype` row lists only the first four. R1 also added messaging columns to `sprk_communication` (ACS ids, thread lookup) that the doc does not describe.</background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file>docs/data-model/sprk_communication.md</file>
      <file>src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Communication/Models/CommunicationType.cs</file>
      <file>src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Communication/CommunicationThreadReadService.cs</file>
    </relevant-files>
    <dependencies>None — independent doc fix (parallel group A).</dependencies>
  </context>
  <constraints>
    <constraint source="project">Documentation-only: do NOT modify any file under `src/`, `tests/`, or `.claude/`. Fix the doc to match code (Code-wins per root CLAUDE.md §2).</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Verify each added column/option against actual code or the as-built schema before writing it — do NOT invent columns. Where a column exists in code but its exact Dataverse attributes are unverifiable from the repo, describe conservatively and flag it in notes.</constraint>
  </constraints>
  <knowledge>
    <files>
      <file>docs/data-model/sprk_communication.md</file>
    </files>
    <patterns>
      <pattern name="CommunicationType source of truth" location="src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Communication/Models/CommunicationType.cs">The enum is the authoritative option-set integer list for `sprk_communicationtype`.</pattern>
    </patterns>
  </knowledge>
  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="1">Diff the doc's `sprk_communicationtype` options against `CommunicationType.cs`; confirm `Message = 100000004` is the missing value.</step>
    <step order="2">Grep the code for R1 messaging columns on `sprk_communication` (ACS message id, ACS thread id, the `sprk_communicationthread` lookup, and any other R1 messaging additions actually referenced) to build the verified list of missing columns.</step>
    <step order="3">Add the `100000004: Message` option to the `sprk_communicationtype` row and add table rows for each verified missing R1 column (logical name, schema name, type, short description).</step>
    <step order="4">Update the doc's review header (Last Reviewed date + a one-line note crediting the R3 doc-drift correction).</step>
    <step order="5">Update `projects/messaging-communication-app-r3/tasks/TASK-INDEX.md` status for 006 to ✅.</step>
    <step order="6">Record any column that could not be fully verified from the repo in `projects/messaging-communication-app-r3/notes/`.</step>
  </steps>
  <escalation><trigger>If a purportedly-missing R1 column cannot be confirmed from code or the as-built schema in the repo, STOP short of inventing it — document the gap in notes and escalate per root CLAUDE.md §6 rather than guessing attributes.</trigger></escalation>
